      ":question/id": "1ff473d5-a7de-5679-980c-c5fa4e5df5b9",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-10289",
      ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of  $f(x)=4{x}^{6}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the constant multiple and power rules, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{6}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 6{x}^{6-1} \\\\  & =24{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186233469,
