      ":question/id": "9342c495-5eb7-5bb2-becb-1daa8a37b8ad",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142993",
      ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $h(x).$\n\n${h}^{'}(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
