      ":question/id": "ba3e5599-fc73-5d06-ba59-ef92cf39216b",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-167561",
      ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $g(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${g}^{\u2032}(x)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{x}-1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)} \\\\  & ={x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
